t we didn't really get to  rehearse  it seems with each other no so we never  knew what to expect um if i had a scene  with ansel or mike  we would just show up and i was like i  don't know what they're about to do they  might screw me over i don't know what  they have on their mind right now so i  feel like we were definitely all on our  toes waiting to see what the other  person would do which is so realistic  because that's that's what it's a real  conversation in real life if you were  put in the situation you're always kind  of on guard waiting to see what the  other person is going to do and i think  that kind of shows you know yeah but we  had been spending months together  building this thing uh even though we  hadn't gotten to those actual scenes or  storytelling elements yet um  we were very much aware of each other  and  the essence of what each other's person  was and their character was and and  just getting it was that build up that i  think was like oh we're about to you  know get excited to see this thing yeah  yeah and build and building trust and  like because  the like between david and i like that's  a weird relationship on on camera  especially like during the rumble and  like the fact that we were able to have  a relationship outside of that build  some trust and then know that when we  were showing to the rumble like we were  not friends we we were not ansel and  david we were bernardo and tony and but  then at the same time i remember one  time one of my punches didn't go to the  right place and i kind of hit you but  because you love me and because there  was love there  you were like damn bro you got me but  it's all good  [Laughter]  and and finally guys you know  myself being a theater nerd watching it  from the prologue  like the moment you start to see um even  like nods to the old choreography but  then seeing how the new stuff blends in  and makes its own mark was a thrill i'm  curious for the three of you when you  watched it on screen for the first time  knowing the amount of work and passion  that went into it what was your first  reaction  i don't know i feel like we can  i feel like we all kind of had a similar  reaction where we thought that  everything else was perfect except for  ourselves  like when i saw it i thought everything  was perfect except for what i did and  then you thought the same thing yeah and  then you thought the same thing so  i feel like it was kind of interesting  to  to see that because we we just had to  process it because i feel like we went  in to see it and we're gonna like  criticize ourselves we're like what did  i do wrong what did i do right and then  you gotta learn to just not do that you  gotta learn to just sit there and and  enjoy it like another audience member  would um  and just take it for what it is and then  once you do that you  start seeing the beauty of everything  you know  the bigger picture yeah yeah it was  really comforting though like in terms  of i mean going with the whole ensemble  thing comforting knowing like like when  we were on the car and we were all  thinking the same thing we said out loud  no no you're amazing i suck  maybe none of us  [Laughter]  or we all suck  that's awesome well i'm gonna go with  you we're all good because i gotta go  now guys it was a pleasure and uh i  can't wait to watch the movie again  honestly congratulations thank you so  much

